## 7. Technology Decisions

### 7.1 Why Python?
- Rich ecosystem for data processing
- Excellent libraries for graph analysis (NetworkX)
- Strong template engines (Jinja2)
- Easy integration with Git

### 7.2 Why Streamlit?
- Rapid UI development
- Reactive programming model
- No frontend JavaScript required
- Built-in components for forms and tables

### 7.3 Why NetworkX?
- Mature graph library
- Comprehensive algorithms
- Well-documented
- Excellent performance for our scale

### 7.4 Why File-Based Storage?
- Simple deployment (no database server)
- Git-friendly (text-based YAML)
- Human-readable for audits
- Easy backup and portability

---

## 8. Performance Considerations

### 8.1 Graph Operations
- In-memory graph for fast queries
- Rebuild only when items change
- Caching for expensive operations
- Target: < 1 second for 1000 items

### 8.2 Document Generation
- Template caching
- Incremental version updates
- Parallel processing for multiple documents
- Target: < 10 seconds for 100 items

### 8.3 UI Responsiveness
- Lazy loading for large datasets
- Pagination for tables
- Async operations where possible
- Target: < 1 second for page loads

---

## 9. Security Considerations

### 9.1 Data Integrity
- Schema validation before save
- Git commit signatures
- File system permissions
- Audit trail via Git history

### 9.2 Access Control
- User authentication (future)
- Role-based permissions (future)
- Currently: file system permissions

